1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,525
Overlays, atlases, and time series.

2
00:00:02,525 --> 00:00:10,099
Compare aligned images, inspect a bold signal over time, and use atlas labels as references.

3
00:00:10,099 --> 00:00:15,148
The goal is clear: Configure overlay opacity and color maps.

4
00:00:15,998 --> 00:00:18,762
One coordinate, several sources of evidence.

5
00:00:18,762 --> 00:00:23,368
Overlays let you compare images in the same coordinate space.

6
00:00:23,368 --> 00:00:27,514
Time-series plots show how a voxel changes across volumes.

7
00:00:27,514 --> 00:00:37,648
Atlas lookup adds an anatomical label, but atlas boundaries are probabilistic and should not be treated as ground truth for every participant.

8
00:00:37,648 --> 00:00:44,096
Registration quality control is easiest when boundaries from two images can be seen together.

9
00:00:44,096 --> 00:00:48,242
Alternate visibility, adjust opacity, or use an edge overlay.

10
00:00:48,242 --> 00:00:56,994
For functional data, look for sudden spikes, drifts, or dropout and relate them to later motion and preprocessing reports.

11
00:00:57,844 --> 00:01:01,425
Now connect the idea to an observable check.

12
00:01:01,425 --> 00:01:06,348
First, load an anatomical background and a functional or standard-space overlay.

13
00:01:06,348 --> 00:01:08,138
Next, reduce overlay opacity.

14
00:01:08,138 --> 00:01:12,166
Then, check alignment in at least three distant locations.

15
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:17,537
After that, open atlas tools and note the probability for one label.

16
00:01:17,537 --> 00:01:21,565
Record what you observe so the decision remains reviewable.

17
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:23,808
Quality Control Check.

18
00:01:23,808 --> 00:01:26,593
Inspect multiple slices and brain boundaries.

19
00:01:26,593 --> 00:01:31,700
Do not accept registration because the images overlap near the center.

20
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:39,129
A useful self-check is this: Why is a single central slice insufficient for registration quality control?

21
00:01:39,129 --> 00:01:46,557
Misalignment can be local or more visible near boundaries; several planes and regions must be inspected.

22
00:01:47,407 --> 00:01:52,195
To recap: First, use overlays to test spatial correspondence.

23
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:56,982
Next, atlas labels are references, not perfect individual anatomy.

24
00:01:56,982 --> 00:02:04,961
Before continuing, make sure you can explain this objective: Configure overlay opacity and color maps.
